  "notes": [
   "Every supplier row maps one-to-one to an RFx line (30 of 30), matched by size, ply, flute, GSM, BF and print. Supplier S/N order differs from RFx line order: S/N 1-3 are the printed items (RFx 23-25) and S/N 26-30 are partitions, sheet, pad and edge guard (RFx 28, 29, 26, 27, 30).",
   "No spec deviations found. The supplier does not state flute for the printed and 7-ply items, or the print sides, but the sizes match uniquely.",
   "Terms differ from the RFx: prices are in USD, not INR; FCA Bhiwandi, not DAP Chakan; freight is extra at USD 850 per shipment (about 4 shipments per month, recorded as 48 per year); payment is 45 days from invoice, not 60 days from GRN; validity is 60 days, not 90.",
   "The Total cell (Commercial Offer!H39) and the Ext. Value column are empty, so no totals were recorded.",
   "Prices are converted to INR at invoicing (SBI TT selling rate), so the INR amount depends on the exchange rate on the invoice date. This is recorded as written.",
   "Lead time days are recorded as 15 (the less favourable printed-item figure). The unit is working days, not calendar days.",
   "The ISO 9001 certificate expires 2028-01-14, before the contract ends on 2028-03-31. The FSC certificate is valid through 2029-06-19.",
   "Q3 was answered yes: in-house testing is confirmed and a CoA is given with every lot. Q10 gave only counts of customers, with names on request, so no boolean was set."
